    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0475" n="369" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg369"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                    Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                        1901</hi></date>,</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 382.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of Mr.
                    Squier’s dispatch, No. 674, of July 22 last,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d345-f1"/>
                    inclosing a copy of correspondence regarding a proposed revision of the code of
                    rules for the mixed court at Shanghai, and reporting that he has requested the
                    United States consul-general at Shanghai to confer with his British and German
                    colleagues with the view of drafting a revised code for submission to the
                    diplomatic body.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to say that the department would be glad to examine the proposed
                    code after it has been agreed upon by the consuls.,</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
